  "output": {
    "section_id": "ch05.s13",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "ch05.s13.p01",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p01.01",
            "text": "How can you tell whether fine-tuning actually worked, and whether the model learned the task without simply overfitting the training data?",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p01.02",
            "text": "After training, the training loss reaches about 0.083, the validation loss reaches about 0.074, the training accuracy improves to around 100%, and the validation accuracy reaches 97.5%.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2022",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2025",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2029",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2032",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2035"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p01.03",
            "text": "As the model sees more examples, both the training loss and the validation loss go down.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2042",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2045",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2049",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2051",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2054"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p01.04",
            "text": "Very low training loss and very low validation loss, together with no noticeable gap between them, indicate good training with little to no overfitting.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2055",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2057",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2059",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2061",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2063",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2066",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2068",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2070",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2072",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2074",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2076",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2078"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p01.05",
            "text": "If the validation loss is much higher than the training loss, that is a sign of overfitting.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2081",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2083",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2084",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2086",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2087"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p01.06",
            "text": "The accuracy plot follows the same pattern: as loss decreases, training accuracy rises to 1 and validation accuracy rises to about 97%.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2090",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2091",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2093",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2095",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2097",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2099",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2101",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2103"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch05.s13.p02",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p02.01",
            "text": "Those plotted accuracies need one important qualification.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p02.02",
            "text": "Because the evaluation iteration was set to five, the plotted accuracy values are not representative of performance on the entire dataset.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2105",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2108",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2110",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2117",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2119",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2121",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2123",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2125"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p02.03",
            "text": "During training, the training and validation performance shown in those plots was based on only five batches for efficiency.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2125",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2128",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2130",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2131"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p02.04",
            "text": "To measure performance on the full training, validation, and test sets, run the \"calculate_accuracy_loader\" function with a data loader, the model, and the device.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2134",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2136",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2138",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2140",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2143",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2144",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2147",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2148",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2150"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p02.05",
            "text": "The \"calculate_accuracy_loader\" function uses the model to make predictions, compares them with the actual values, reports accuracy, and does this over all batches in the dataset rather than only five batches.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2153",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2156",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2161",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2164",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2166",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2168",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2170",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2172",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2174"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p02.06",
            "text": "Accuracy measured over all batches in the training, validation, and test sets is a better representative measure than the plots based on only five evaluation batches.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2178",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2180",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2182",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2184",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2186",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2188",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2189"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch05.s13.p03",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p03.01",
            "text": "With that fuller evaluation, the picture changes slightly.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p03.02",
            "text": "On the full datasets, the training accuracy is 97%, the validation accuracy is 97%, and the test accuracy is 95%.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2193",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2195",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2197",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2198",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2200",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2204",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2205"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p03.03",
            "text": "A small gap where test accuracy is slightly lower than training accuracy suggests a small amount of overfitting.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2205",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2208",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2211",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2213",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2215",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2217",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2218",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2220",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2222",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2224",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2226"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p03.04",
            "text": "Validation accuracy is often somewhat higher than test accuracy because model development often involves fine-tuning parameters on the validation set.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2227",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2230",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2231",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2233",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2235"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p03.05",
            "text": "That validation-test gap could potentially be reduced by adjusting model settings such as increasing the dropout rate or the optimizer's weight decay parameter.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2238",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2241",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2242",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2244",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2246"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p03.06",
            "text": "This setup leaves room to experiment with dropout rate, learning rate, weight decay, and which parameters are unfrozen during fine-tuning.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2248",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2251",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2252",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2255",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2257",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2259",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2260",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2262",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2266",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2267"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p03.07",
            "text": "In the current setup, the trained parameters are the output classification head, the last transformer block, and the final normalization layer.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2269",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2272",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2274",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2276",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2277",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2279",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2281"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p03.08",
            "text": "One possible experiment is to train more transformer blocks instead of only the last one.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2281",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2284",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2285",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2287"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch05.s13.p04",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p04.r01",
            "text": "These results also highlight the trade-offs of fine-tuning.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p04.r02",
            "text": "In this project, training reduced the loss and increased the accuracy.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2744",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2746",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2747"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p04.r03",
            "text": "A disadvantage of fine-tuning is that it requires additional training time on a specific dataset.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2761",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2764",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2766",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2769",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2771",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2772"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p04.r04",
            "text": "An advantage is that the model becomes specialized to the target dataset, here the spam collection, and can act as a spam classifier.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2775",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2777",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2779",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2782",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2784",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2785",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2788"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p04.r05",
            "text": "The same fine-tuning code can be applied to a wide range of classification tasks and datasets.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2880",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2881",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2884",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2885"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p04.r06",
            "text": "Classification fine-tuning is one category of fine-tuning, and another major category is instruction fine-tuning.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2911",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2914",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2916",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2918",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2921",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2922"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p04.r07",
            "text": "Instruction fine-tuning can be used to build a chatbot that answers or replies to specific instructions.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2922",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2924",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2927",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2929"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s13.p04.r08",
            "text": "This approach opens research opportunities both in changing and testing LLM architectures and in applying them to classification projects.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2953",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2955",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2958",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2959",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2962",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2964",
              "0PpxZ3kNPWo@2966"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
